  "question": {
    "text": "The $\\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{sp}}$ of $\\mathrm{CuS}, \\mathrm{Ag}_{2} \\mathrm{~S}$ and $\\mathrm{HgS}$ are $10^{-31}, 10^{-44}$ and $10^{-54}$ respectively. The solubility of these sulphides are in the order :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "vo6FH",
      "text": "$\\quad \\mathrm{Ag}_{2} \\mathrm{~S}>\\mathrm{CuS}>\\mathrm{HgS}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "gXI1F",
      "text": "$\\quad \\mathrm{AgS}>\\mathrm{HgS}>\\mathrm{CuS}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GBik3",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{HgS}>\\mathrm{Ag}_{2} \\mathrm{~S}>\\mathrm{CuS}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "iwjoz",
      "text": "$\\quad\\mathrm{CuS}>\\mathrm{Ag}_{2} \\mathrm{~S}>\\mathrm{HgS}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "For CuS, solubility $=\\left(10^{-31}\\right)^{1 / 2}$;\n$$\n\\begin{array}{l}\n\\text { For } \\mathrm{Ag}_{2} \\mathrm{~S}=\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{sp}}}{4}\\right)^{\\frac{1}{3}}=\\left(\\frac{10^{-44}}{4}\\right)^{\\frac{1}{3}} \\text { and } \\\\\n\\text { for } \\mathrm{HgS}=\\left(10^{-54}\\right)^{\\frac{1}{2}}\n\\end{array}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
